**suggestion (bug_risk):** Avoid duplicating the namespace column in `conflictTarget` when the caller already includes it.

If `params.conflictTarget` already includes the namespace column, this will prepend `col` again (e.g. `['__ns', '__ns', 'id']`), which may cause SQL errors or undefined behavior depending on the driver. Normalize `conflictTarget` to unique columns (e.g. `Array.from(new Set([col, ...conflictTarget]))`) so `col` appears exactly once.

```suggestion
      const create = stampData(params.create, col, params.namespace!);
      const update = removeColumnFromData(params.update, col);
      // Augment conflict target to include namespace column for composite PK,
      // ensuring the namespace column appears at most once
      let conflictTarget = params.conflictTarget;
      if (conflictTarget) {
        const targets = Array.isArray(conflictTarget)
          ? conflictTarget
          : [conflictTarget];

        conflictTarget = Array.from(new Set([col, ...targets]));
      }
```

