**suggestion (bug_risk):** Clarify or remove the `$onDuplicateKeyUpdate` check in the MySQL upsert branch.

In the MySQL branch, `db.insert(tbl).values(create as any).$onDuplicateKeyUpdate` will almost certainly be falsy: Drizzle exposes `onDuplicateKeyUpdate` as a method, not a `$onDuplicateKeyUpdate` property. That means this branch is effectively dead code. If you want to feature-detect `onDuplicateKeyUpdate`, please base it on a documented API or dialect/version check; otherwise, consider removing this guard and always calling `onDuplicateKeyUpdate` (or just using a plain insert) to avoid confusion.

```suggestion
        if (config.dialect === 'mysql') {
          // Drizzle exposes `onDuplicateKeyUpdate` as a method, not a `$onDuplicateKeyUpdate` property;
          // use it only when we actually have update data, otherwise fall back to a plain insert.
          const q = hasUpdate
            ? db.insert(tbl).values(create as any).onDuplicateKeyUpdate({ set: update as any })
            : db.insert(tbl).values(create as any);
```

